WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.880
When speaking or using a touchscreen is difficult. a simple message can be hard to

2
00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:07.339
express.

3
00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:10.091
CareSwitch is a student communication prototype.

4
00:00:10.091 --> 00:00:15.136
This edited demonstration uses actual mouse-mode screen captures. with synthetic
narration.

5
00:00:15.136 --> 00:00:18.806
Live head tracking is explained. not recorded here.

6
00:00:19.406 --> 00:00:26.144
For someone who can comfortably move their head. a helper can enable the camera and

7
00:00:26.144 --> 00:00:27.941
follow five movement-range prompts.

8
00:00:27.941 --> 00:00:32.433
A pretrained MediaPipe model finds face landmarks on the device.

9
00:00:32.433 --> 00:00:35.577
Calibration maps movement into an in-app pointer.

10
00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:38.722
This is head control. not eye-gaze tracking.

11
00:00:39.322 --> 00:00:46.211
The board provides six editable messages for a care conversation. including yes. no.
and I

12
00:00:46.211 --> 00:00:47.588
need a break.

13
00:00:47.588 --> 00:00:53.099
Camera control uses a timed hold; mouse. keyboard and touch offer alternatives.

14
00:00:53.699 --> 00:00:57.055
Selecting I need a break creates a draft.

15
00:00:57.055 --> 00:01:01.670
The exact phrase appears for review. and nothing is spoken yet.

16
00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:04.187
Confirm and Cancel are separate choices.

17
00:01:04.187 --> 00:01:09.221
In head mode. the pointer must leave the first target before confirming.

18
00:01:09.821 --> 00:01:14.826
After confirmation. the chosen message appears as the final message.

19
00:01:14.826 --> 00:01:18.830
If playback fails. the confirmed text remains visible.

20
00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:21.833
Read again lets the user retry.

21
00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:26.838
CareSwitch reads the user's choice. rather than generating medical advice.

22
00:01:27.438 --> 00:01:33.852
Prepared messages cover English. Urdu. Arabic. Hindi. Spanish. French. German and
Chinese.

23
00:01:33.852 --> 00:01:38.662
A matching local device voice is used when available.

24
00:01:38.662 --> 00:01:45.076
A bundled free speech engine provides a fallback without a paid API.

25
00:01:45.076 --> 00:01:47.749
Pronunciation still needs fluent-speaker review.

26
00:01:48.349 --> 00:01:52.142
Hold time. sensitivity and smoothing can be adjusted.

27
00:01:52.142 --> 00:01:55.936
Filtering and a speed limit steady the pointer.

28
00:01:55.936 --> 00:02:00.677
Missing faces. multiple faces or stale tracking stop dwell selection.

29
00:02:00.677 --> 00:02:04.471
Users can also force the free built-in voice.

30
00:02:05.071 --> 00:02:10.438
A helper can edit the phrases or use mouse and keyboard.

31
00:02:10.438 --> 00:02:13.365
The responsive layout also supports touch.

32
00:02:13.365 --> 00:02:15.805
Setup instructions are currently English.

33
00:02:15.805 --> 00:02:21.172
Physical-phone performance. comfort and accessibility still need testing with real
users.

34
00:02:21.772 --> 00:02:26.457
Camera frames are not recorded or uploaded by the app.

35
00:02:26.457 --> 00:02:28.799
There is no patient database.

36
00:02:28.799 --> 00:02:33.952
The caregiver phrase speaks a request; it does not contact anyone.

37
00:02:33.952 --> 00:02:38.168
CareSwitch does not diagnose. prescribe or send emergency alerts.

38
00:02:38.168 --> 00:02:40.978
It has not been clinically validated.

39
00:02:41.578 --> 00:02:44.791
AI tools helped build the prototype.

40
00:02:44.791 --> 00:02:50.681
The next step is feedback from intended users and accessibility specialists.

41
00:02:50.681 --> 00:02:53.894
Try CareSwitch using the project link.

42
00:02:53.894 --> 00:02:54.964
Your movement.

43
00:02:54.964 --> 00:02:56.035
Your message.
